  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "certificate",
      "title": "Enrollment type and identity method",
      "items": [
        "Automated Device Enrollment, account-driven enrollment, and profile-based enrollment describe how enrollment begins. SCEP and ACME describe how the device obtains its identity.",
        "Account-driven discovery selects User Enrollment (mdm-byod) or Device Enrollment (mdm-adde). The reference server\u2019s OTA delivery supports SCEP only and separates identity bootstrap from MDM profile delivery."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "authentication",
      "title": "Discovery and trust",
      "items": [
        "/MDMServiceConfig advertises the ADE URL and trust-anchor URL. A trust-profile URL is included only when HTTPS anchors are configured.",
        "Account-driven discovery uses /.well-known/com.apple.remotemanagement. HTTPS trust anchors are configured independently of identity issuers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "success",
      "title": "Common outcome",
      "items": [
        "Profiles use stable stored identifiers and advertise per-user connections. The device obtains its certificate, then checks in and supplies push details.",
        "Controlled replacement updates an existing enrollment through a separate authorized handshake; see the companion sequence."
      ]
    },
    {
